Author:     Fabricio Breve <fbreve@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Fri Aug 14 17:57:37 2026 -0300
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: Sat Aug 15 04:57:37 2026 +0800

    Refine Codemasters mapper handling and add Game Gear EEPROM support (#199)
    
    * Refine Codemasters mapper handling
    
    Allows the detection of "Heroes Against Demons" (SMS). No need to force Sega mapper anymore.
    Codemasters detection was too agressive and could mistakenly identify non-Codemasters games like this one.
    
    Restrict Codemasters-related bank writes to valid memory requests and rely on static/forced detection before accepting them. This also removes the BIOS handoff locking path from the Codemasters write handlers and updates the related mapper comments.
    
    * Add Game Gear EEPROM cart support
    
    Implement 93C46 EEPROM cartridge support for the Game Gear baseball titles that use it. This adds EEPROM mapper hardware, CRC32-based cart detection, NVRAM initialization to 0xFF, bus/memory routing in the main system, and savestate save/restore coverage so EEPROM-backed saves persist correctly.
    
    New games supported:
    - Hyper Pro Yakyuu '92 (Japan)
    - Pro Yakyuu GG League (Japan)
    - Majors, The - Pro Baseball (USA)
    - World Series Baseball (USA)
    - World Series Baseball (USA) (Rev A)
    - World Series Baseball '95 (USA)
    - World Series Baseball '95 (USA) (Beta) (1994-06-29)
    - World Series Baseball '95 (USA) (Beta) (1994-07-09)
    - World Series Baseball '95 (USA) (Beta) (1994-07-19)
    - World Series Baseball '95 (USA) (Beta) (1994-07-22)
    - World Series Baseball '95 (USA) (Beta) (1994-07-28)
    - World Series Baseball '95 (USA) (Beta) (1994-07-29)
    
    This commit fixes issue #130

